dramatically|great-degree-or-sudden-change|ADVERB|great degree or striking change|to a very great or noticeable degree, often with a striking change|một cách rõ rệt|Visitor numbers increased dramatically after the museum reopened.|Lượng khách tăng lên đáng kể sau khi bảo tàng mở cửa trở lại.|Adverb; modifies a verb, adjective, or other adverb.|dramatically
cavity|hole-or-space|NOUN|hollow space|a hollow space inside something|khoang rỗng; hốc|Researchers found a small cavity inside the rock.|Các nhà nghiên cứu phát hiện một khoảng rỗng nhỏ bên trong khối đá.|Count noun; commonly followed by in or within when locating the hollow space.|cavity
restrain|physically-stop|VERB|physically hold back|to use physical force to hold someone or something back or prevent movement|giữ lại bằng sức lực|Two officers restrained the man near the station entrance.|Hai cảnh sát giữ người đàn ông lại gần lối vào nhà ga.|Transitive verb; restrain someone from doing something.|restrain
jurisdiction|legal-authority|NOUN|legal authority|the legal authority to make decisions or take action in a particular area or case|thẩm quyền pháp lý|The local court has no jurisdiction over the dispute.|Tòa án địa phương không có thẩm quyền xét xử tranh chấp này.|Uncountable noun in the general sense; often jurisdiction over a case or area.|jurisdiction
landscape|appearance-of-an-area|NOUN|appearance of an area|the overall appearance of an area of land|phong cảnh; diện mạo vùng đất|The road offers a clear view of the mountain landscape.|Con đường cho thấy rõ phong cảnh núi non.|Count noun; commonly modified by a word describing the area, such as rural or mountain.|landscape
founder|person-who-establishes|NOUN|person who establishes something|a person who starts an organization, institution, or similar undertaking|người sáng lập|The company's founder returned to speak with the new employees.|Người sáng lập công ty trở lại trò chuyện với các nhân viên mới.|Count noun; often followed by of and the organization or institution.|founder
cowboy|cowboy-source-label|NOUN|cattle worker|a worker whose job includes looking after cattle, often while riding a horse|người chăn bò; cao bồi|The cowboy rode along the fence to check the cattle.|Người chăn bò cưỡi ngựa dọc hàng rào để kiểm tra đàn gia súc.|Count noun; covers the farm-worker sense, not the separate informal UK use for an unreliable trader.|cowboy
bathe|wash-oneself|VERB|wash oneself|to wash your body or part of it with water|tắm rửa|They bathed before sitting down to dinner.|Họ tắm rửa trước khi ngồi vào ăn tối.|Intransitive when referring to washing oneself; bathe in a place or body of water.|bathe
originally|at-the-beginning|ADVERB|at the beginning|at the beginning of a situation or when something first happened|ban đầu|The building was originally a small school.|Ban đầu, tòa nhà này là một ngôi trường nhỏ.|Adverb; commonly precedes the main verb or follows be.|originally
reach|arrive-at-a-place|VERB|arrive at a place|to arrive at a place or destination|đến nơi|We reached the coast before the fog became heavy.|Chúng tôi đến bờ biển trước khi sương mù trở nên dày đặc.|Transitive verb; takes the destination directly without to.|reach
reach|attain-a-level|VERB|attain a level|to get to a particular level, value, or point|đạt tới mức|Attendance reached its highest level in May.|Số người tham dự đạt mức cao nhất vào tháng Năm.|Transitive verb; takes the level or value directly as its object.|reach
reach|within-touching-distance|NOUN|distance within which one can touch|the distance within which someone can touch or access something|tầm với|Leave the spare key where you can easily reach it.|Hãy để chìa khóa dự phòng ở nơi bạn có thể dễ dàng lấy.|Uncountable noun in this use; common phrases include within reach and out of reach.|reach
golf|club-and-ball-sport|NOUN|club-and-ball sport|a sport in which players use clubs to hit a small ball toward a series of holes|môn gôn|My parents play golf together every Sunday.|Bố mẹ tôi cùng chơi gôn vào mỗi Chủ nhật.|Uncountable noun for the sport; play golf does not normally take an article.|golf
sue|take-someone-to-court|VERB|take legal action|to start legal action against someone, often because of harm or a loss|kiện; khởi kiện|The tenant sued the company for failing to repair the roof.|Người thuê nhà kiện công ty vì không sửa mái nhà.|Transitive verb; sue someone for something or for doing something.|sue
partiality|preference-or-bias|NOUN|preference or bias|a preference for one person or thing over another, sometimes unfairly|sự thiên vị; sở thích thiên lệch|The referee was warned not to show partiality to either team.|Trọng tài được nhắc không thiên vị đội nào.|Uncountable noun; partiality for something and show partiality are common patterns.|partiality
draft|unfinished-written-version|NOUN|unfinished written version|an early written version that has not yet been completed or finalized|bản nháp|She sent the first draft of her report to her manager.|Cô gửi bản nháp đầu tiên của báo cáo cho quản lý.|Count noun; commonly a draft of a report or document.|draft
draft|prepare-a-document|VERB|prepare a document|to prepare a written version of a document or agreement|soạn thảo|The lawyers drafted a short agreement for both sides.|Các luật sư soạn một thỏa thuận ngắn cho cả hai bên.|Transitive verb; draft a document, proposal, or agreement.|draft
track|running-course|NOUN|running course|a prepared path or circuit used for running|đường chạy|The runners warmed up on the track before the race.|Các vận động viên khởi động trên đường chạy trước cuộc đua.|Count noun; this sense is a running course, not railway rails or a music recording.|track
track|railway-rails|NOUN|railway route|the rails and prepared route on which a train travels|đường ray|Workers inspected the railway track before service resumed.|Công nhân kiểm tra đường ray trước khi tàu chạy lại.|Count noun; commonly railway track or tracks.|track
track|music-recording|NOUN|recorded music piece|one recorded piece of music on an album or other recording|bản nhạc trong album|Her favorite track comes near the end of the album.|Bản nhạc cô thích nằm gần cuối album.|Count noun in music; a track on an album.|track
track|monitor-progress|VERB|monitor or record progress|to keep a record of something or follow its progress over time|theo dõi|The app tracks how many steps I take each day.|Ứng dụng theo dõi số bước tôi đi mỗi ngày.|Transitive verb; track someone's progress or track a quantity over time.|track
solution|answer-to-a-problem|NOUN|answer to a problem|a way of solving a problem or dealing with a difficult situation|giải pháp|They found a practical solution to the parking problem.|Họ tìm được cách giải quyết thiết thực cho vấn đề đỗ xe.|Count noun; solution to a problem.|solution
solution|liquid-mixture|NOUN|liquid mixture|a liquid in which one or more substances have been dissolved|dung dịch|Stir the solution until all the salt has dissolved.|Khuấy dung dịch cho đến khi toàn bộ muối tan.|Count noun; solution of a substance or a solution containing it.|solution
nobody|no-person|PRONOUN|no person|not any person; no one|không một ai|Nobody knew why the lights had gone out.|Không ai biết vì sao đèn bị tắt.|Singular pronoun; it takes a singular verb and usually appears without a negative verb.|nobody
beforehand|in-advance|ADVERB|in advance|before a particular time or event|trước đó; từ trước|We booked the tickets beforehand to avoid the queue.|Chúng tôi đặt vé trước để tránh phải xếp hàng.|Adverb; often placed at the end of a clause.|beforehand
natural|not-made-by-people|ADJECTIVE|not made by people|existing in nature rather than made by people|tự nhiên; không nhân tạo|Many birds return to their natural habitat each spring.|Nhiều loài chim trở lại môi trường sống tự nhiên vào mỗi mùa xuân.|Attributive adjective before a noun; this sense concerns origin, not an unforced manner.|natural
natural|unforced-or-easy|ADJECTIVE|unforced manner|relaxed and not appearing forced or artificial|tự nhiên; không gượng ép|She felt more natural speaking with a small group.|Cô cảm thấy tự nhiên hơn khi nói chuyện với một nhóm nhỏ.|Predicative adjective after feel, look, or sound; describes manner, not origin.|natural
southern|in-or-of-the-south|ADJECTIVE|in or of the south|located in, directed toward, or associated with the south|phía nam; thuộc phương nam|They moved to a southern region near the coast.|Họ chuyển đến một vùng phía nam gần bờ biển.|Attributive adjective before a noun; describes a relative direction, without naming a country.|southern
